Asymmetric reserve allocation in the affine local-moment bound
Exact boundary: 8748673/10000000. Date: 13 October 2026.

New asymmetric reserve allocation, rational geometry/certificate adaptations,
and explanatory note: Zhongpai Gao, with AI assistance. Apache-2.0.

The affine capacity is by Kari Roegnvaldsson, reused from accepted tracker
submission affine-local-20261013 at c707738a659786b9a44a79c629bed8c801cca8f3.
The preceding reserve-reallocation source is pinned to PR 38 at
14ab1618c5133a7d12e06aa76661bbcb34e843cd. That source was an unverified
candidate at preparation; the current adaptation has separate checks.

The complete local 22/5 analytic proof is by nielstron, at source commit
16ce30342471344c2b2f0d383388e6f9acb9bccf. Mathematical predecessors include
OpenAI's quasi-Riemann development fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb,
Akash Levy's weighted numerator 2fd60c0926b66ea18d7436f5ed55250fd006ab5d,
Hailey Collet's Cycle25 development, and Zhongpai Gao's earlier local-moment
adapters 44e93fbcac36bfd10cc1316674c970747888d448.

